    "march.testimonial.label": "Testimonial",
    "march.testimonial.before": "\u201CThe night before the march, we gathered in a small kitchen in Coyoacan to paint our signs. My grandmother\u2019s hands, steady at eighty-two, traced the words \u2018Ni Una Menos\u2019 in purple ink. She told us about the women who walked these same streets decades ago, how their voices were swallowed by silence. Tomorrow, she said, the city will hear us.\u201D",
    "march.testimonial.after": "\u201CWhen we returned home that evening, my feet aching and my voice nearly gone, I sat on the curb and cried. Not from exhaustion, but from the overwhelming feeling that something had shifted. My daughter, only seven, looked at me and said, \u2018Mama, will we march again next year?\u2019 I held her close and whispered, \u2018Every year, mija, until we don\u2019t have to anymore.\u2019\u201D",
    "march.before.desc1": "Majo & Mafer",
    "march.before.desc2": "Helen & Caridad",
    "march.before.testimony1": "Majo and Mafer from Mexico City shared their experience participating in Women's Day marches. Majo started in 2020 and Mafer in 2023, advocating for equity, respect, and an end to gender-based violence. Both emphasized the unity and emotional significance of the movement.",
    "march.before.testimony2": "Helen and Caridad joined the 8M march in Mexico City. Helen feels more confident in her second march, surrounded by supportive women. Caridad marches to address machismo after realizing its impact and wants to contribute to change.",
