    "march.during.desc9": "Denunciar a su violador",
    "march.during.testimony1": "Hannah Gonz\u00E1lez, a model, marches to support women in the movement of art models in resistance who have faced violence in artistic spaces. Her main message at the march is respect.",
    "march.during.testimony2": "The Gordofobia collective joined the 8M march in Mexico City for the first time as a group, performing with their bodies and ropes as an activation against fatphobia. They chanted phrases like 'No to fat hate' and encouraged 'fat solidarity'.",
    "march.during.testimony3": "\u00C1ngeles, from Mexico City, joins the march as a survivor of domestic violence and mother seeking justice following a rape. She demands justice and emphasizes children's honesty in abuse cases.",
    "march.during.testimony4": "Valeria marched in Mexico City for gender equality, advocating for equal opportunities and safe environments for women. Her key word during the march was 'equality'.",
    "march.during.testimony5": "Brenda, from Mexico City, joins the 8M march for the first time. She feels deeply moved by the event's energy and is marching for her daughter and personal experiences involving violence and abortion in her past.",
    "march.during.testimony6": "Kimberly, Carolina, and Melissa joined the 8M march in Mexico City with varying past experiences. Kimberly and Carolina are participating for the fourth time, while Melissa, joined by her mother, is attending her second march. They aim to highlight injustices in Mexico, support victims, and advocate for better protective laws for women.",
    "march.during.testimony7": "Monserrat Mendoza, attending her fourth 8M march in Mexico City, demands justice after being a victim of sexual assault by a psychology student last October. She condemns the lack of legal and institutional action, voicing the call for 'justice'.",
    "march.during.testimony8": "Francisco, also known as Esot\u00E9rica, marched for the first time in Mexico City after living 52 years in the United States. He emphasized women's resilience, comparing them to the axolotl, and reflected on the violence faced by cis and trans women, highlighting their strength and courage in adversity.",
    "march.during.testimony9": "Montserrat Mendoza, a woman from Mexico, marched for the fourth time on March 8th to demand justice after being sexually assaulted by a psychology student, whose actions remain unpunished. She shared her story, highlighting legal and institutional barriers that have hindered accountability, and emphasized her key message: justice.",
